---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="ImageTool privacy policy: 100% on-device image processing with zero cloud uploads, no tracking cookies, and no third-party data sharing."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <main id="main-content" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 space-y-10 text-slate-700">
    <header class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto space-y-3">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 text-blue-700 text-xs font-semibold uppercase">
        Verified On-Device Privacy
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">
        Privacy Policy &amp; Security Architecture
      </h1>
      <p class="text-slate-600 text-base leading-relaxed">
        Last updated: November 2026. ImageTool was engineered from day one to guarantee that your images, pixels, and file metadata never leave your computer.
      </p>
    </header>

    {/* P-01 to P-04 Guarantees */}
    <section class="p-6 sm:p-8 bg-[#f8f9fc] rounded-xl border border-slate-200/90 shadow-2xs space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">
        Our Core Privacy Commitments (P-01 to P-04)
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-1">
            P-01: Zero Image Pixel Uploads
          </h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600">
            When you select an image, its raw bytes are transferred directly into an isolated background Web Worker on your device. The image is decoded and processed in local memory. At no point are your image bytes or pixels ever transmitted across the internet.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-1">
            P-02: 100% Local Neural AI Inference
          </h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600">
            Our machine learning models (BiRefNet-lite, MODNet, Swin2SR, Real-ESRGAN) execute on your graphics card via WebGPU or your CPU via WebAssembly. Model weights are downloaded to your browser once, but your personal photos are never sent to remote inference servers.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-1">
            P-03: No Third-Party Tracking or Analytics
          </h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600">
            ImageTool contains zero third-party tracking scripts, session recording tools, behavioral analytics, or advertising telemetry. We do not use Google Analytics, Meta Pixel, or any commercial tracking SDKs.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-1">
            P-04: Enforced by Technical Architecture
          </h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600">
            Our privacy promises are not just legal statements; they are technically enforced by a strict Content Security Policy (CSP), cross-origin isolation (COOP/COEP), and automated build verification tests that run on every release.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* Information We Collect */}
    <section class="p-6 bg-[#f8f9fc] rounded-xl border border-slate-200/90 shadow-2xs space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">
        Information We Collect
      </h2>
      <p>
        <strong class="text-slate-900">We do not collect personal information.</strong> You do not need to create an account, log in, or provide an email address to use ImageTool. We have no user databases and store no personal records.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you visit our website, standard web server logs may temporarily record connection metadata (such as your IP address, browser user agent, and requested page path) purely for server health and DDoS mitigation.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* Cookies & Browser Storage */}
    <section class="p-6 bg-[#f8f9fc] rounded-xl border border-slate-200/90 shadow-2xs space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">
        Cookies and Local Storage
      </h2>
      <p>
        <strong class="text-slate-900">Cookies:</strong> ImageTool uses no tracking cookies, marketing cookies, or profiling identifiers.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong class="text-slate-900">IndexedDB Cache:</strong> When you run an AI tool, open-source model weights are downloaded and stored in your browser's private Cache API / IndexedDB (<code class="text-blue-700 bg-blue-50 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-xs">transformers-cache</code>). This allows the tool to load instantly on subsequent visits without re-downloading files. You can clear this cache at any time via your browser settings.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* Content Security Policy Notice */}
    <section class="p-6 bg-[#f8f9fc] rounded-xl border border-slate-200/90 shadow-2xs space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">
        Network Security &amp; Content Security Policy
      </h2>
      <p>
        To prevent unauthorized network exfiltration, ImageTool enforces a strict Content Security Policy:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 text-slate-700 font-mono text-xs bg-white p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-slate-200">
        <li>connect-src 'self' blob: data: https://huggingface.co https://*.huggingface.co</li>
        <li>default-src 'self'</li>
        <li>object-src 'none'</li>
        <li>form-action 'none'</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The only external network requests permitted by the browser are fetching static model weight files from verified Hugging Face CDN endpoints.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
